# Style & Accessibility Standards

## WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance

- All text must meet a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 against its background (3:1 for large text ≥18pt).
- Every interactive element must have a visible focus indicator (outline or ring) that does not rely on color alone.
- Use semantic HTML elements (`<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`) over generic `<div>`s.
- Images require descriptive `alt` text. Decorative images use `alt=""` with `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Form inputs must have associated `<label>` elements or `aria-label` attributes.
- ARIA attributes are a last resort — prefer native HTML semantics first.
- All pages must be fully navigable via keyboard (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Escape).

## Responsive Design (Mobile-First)

- Default styles target mobile viewports.
- Breakpoints follow Tailwind defaults:
  - `sm` — 640px
  - `md` — 768px
  - `lg` — 1024px
  - `xl` — 1280px
- Touch targets must be at least 44x44px on mobile.

## Typography

- Use the Geist font family loaded via `next/font/google`.
- Headings follow a modular scale: `text-4xl` / `text-3xl` / `text-2xl` / `text-xl` / `text-lg`.
- Body text uses `text-base` (16px) minimum for readability.
- Line height for body copy: `leading-relaxed` (1.625).

## Color Palette

- Define all colors as CSS custom properties in `globals.css` so dark mode can override them.
- Stick to the `--background` / `--foreground` variable pattern established by the scaffold.
- Accent color should be defined as `--accent` for consistent use across interactive elements.

## Motion & Animation

- Wrap all animations and transitions in a `prefers-reduced-motion` media query:
  ```css
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    *, *::before, *::after {
      animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
      transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    }
  }
  ```
- Prefer `transition` over `animation` for simple state changes.
- Keep durations under 300ms for UI feedback.
